==Enemy==
A much tougher version of [[Kang Roo]], Shadow Boxer K has rapid Area Attacks and more health, giving her the devastating power to plow through your units, though having more knockbacks makes her vulnerable to flinching from raw damage. She is slightly faster than the original Kang Roo, but is slower compared to the likes of [[Doge Dark]] and [[Gory Dark]], who share a movement speed of 30.

==Strategy==
Like most Dark enemies, Shadow Boxer K pushes with extreme force and can't be stalled easily by meatshields or tanks, but is easily countered by either crowd-controllers who impede her with status effects, or by abusing her high knockback count. Any stackable Area Attacker with a range over 250 should have enough firepower to stop her from pushing, with [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza]] being a notable example due to outranging her and dealing Massive Damage to Darks. Alternatively, [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Nobunaga]] or [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] can freeze her in her tracks.

You can use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] or similar Uber Rares if you like, but, as with most Darks, she flinches so often to damage alone to the point where backliners with long attack cycles aren't needed unless crowd-controllers pin them in place. Melee units aren't that safe either, since unless supported, Shadow Boxer K's fast attack cycle and damage means she can potentially demolish them before they hit her.

